---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Shot from '../components/Shot.astro';
import { links, version } from '../data/site';

import repositoryDark from '../assets/shots/repository-dark.png';
import repositoryLight from '../assets/shots/repository-light.png';
import agentsDark from '../assets/shots/agents-dark.png';
import agentsLight from '../assets/shots/agents-light.png';
import diskDark from '../assets/shots/disk-map-dark.png';
import diskLight from '../assets/shots/disk-map-light.png';
import historyDark from '../assets/shots/history-dark.png';
import historyLight from '../assets/shots/history-light.png';

const safety = [
  ['Offer a branch as safe', 'git confirms its commits are already in the default branch, or a pull request merged them.'],
  ['Offer a worktree as safe', 'it has no uncommitted changes and no commits that exist nowhere else.'],
  ['Clear a generated folder', 'it is git-ignored, it is not a symlink, and it is checked again right before it moves to the Trash.'],
  ['Remove anything at all', 'you reviewed the list and confirmed it.'],
  ['Delete for good', 'it is something Lopper itself moved to the Trash, and you asked for it.'],
];

const faq = [
  ['Can it delete my unmerged work?', 'No. A branch or worktree holding commits that exist nowhere else is never offered as safe. If Lopper cannot prove something is merged it shows "needs a look" and leaves the decision to you. Even then, removed branches come back from History at their exact commit.'],
  ['Does it send anything anywhere?', 'No. There is no account, no analytics and no crash reporting, and this site has none either. Lopper runs git, and the GitHub CLI if you have it, on your Mac and reads only the folders you chose.'],
  ['Which AI tools does it understand?', 'Worktrees from Claude Code, Cursor, Codex and Conductor are recognised by their layout and labelled with the tool. Worktrees from anything else are handled as ordinary git worktrees.'],
  ['Why does macOS warn me the first time?', 'The app is not yet signed with an Apple Developer ID, so Gatekeeper asks you to confirm it once. The steps are just below. The source is open, so you can read it or build it yourself.'],
];
---
<Base>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1>keep your repositories light.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Lopper finds the branches, worktrees and generated folders you no longer need, shows the git evidence that each one
          is safe to remove, and lets you undo anything for 30 days.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href={links.download}>Download for macOS</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href={links.repo}>View on GitHub</a>
        </div>
        <p class="fineprint">Version {version}. Needs macOS 14 or later. Open source, MIT licence.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-visual">
        <div class="window">
          <video
            id="hero-video"
            src="/media/hero.mp4"
            poster="/media/hero-poster.jpg"
            width="1280"
            height="800"
            autoplay
            muted
            loop
            playsinline
            preload="metadata"
            aria-label="Lopper in use: the overview, a repository's evidence, the Agents page and the Disk map."
          ></video>
        </div>
        <button class="pause" id="hero-pause" type="button" aria-pressed="false">Pause animation</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="why wrap" data-reveal>
    <h2>Leftovers pile up quietly. One wrong delete costs real work.</h2>
    <div class="why-text">
      <p>
        If you work in many repositories, and especially with AI coding agents, merged branches stay behind, worktrees from
        finished agent runs sit in a folder nobody opens, and every copy of a project carries its own <code>node_modules</code>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Checking each one by hand is slow, so it does not happen. Lopper does the checking, shows what it found, and waits
        for you to confirm a list. Nothing is removed that you have not seen.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="features" class="features wrap">
    <article class="band" data-reveal>
      <div class="band-copy">
        <h2>Every verdict shows its evidence.</h2>
        <p>
          Safe, needs a look, or protected. For each branch and worktree Lopper lists what it checked: already in the main
          branch, merged through a pull request, the remote branch was deleted, nothing exists only on this branch.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="band-shot window">
        <Shot dark={repositoryDark} light={repositoryLight} alt="A repository in Lopper: a table of branches with Safe, Review and Protected verdicts, and the inspector explaining why the selected branch is safe." />
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="band reverse" data-reveal>
      <div class="band-copy">
        <h2>Agents leave worktrees behind. Lopper finds them.</h2>
        <p>
          Worktrees from Claude Code, Cursor, Codex and Conductor, with how old each one is, whether it holds unmerged or
          uncommitted work, and which are finished. Reclaim all the finished ones in one step.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="band-shot window">
        <Shot dark={agentsDark} light={agentsLight} alt="The Agents page: a table of agent worktrees with their state, unmerged work, activity, age and size, and a button to reclaim the finished ones." />
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="band" data-reveal>
      <div class="band-copy">
        <h2>See where the gigabytes went.</h2>
        <p>
          Generated folders and developer caches by project, by kind, or as a map sized by bytes. Clearing moves them to
          the Trash, and the dependencies come back with the reinstall button if you want them.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="band-shot window">
        <Shot dark={diskDark} light={diskLight} alt="The Disk page as a treemap: node_modules, build output and caches sized by bytes, grouped by project, with developer caches below." />
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="band reverse" data-reveal>
      <div class="band-copy">
        <h2>Undo anything for 30 days.</h2>
        <p>
          Every removal is logged with the reason it was safe. Restore one item or a whole cleanup, and branches come back
          at their exact commit.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="band-shot window">
        <Shot dark={historyDark} light={historyLight} alt="History: a chart of space given back per week and a table of removals with the reason each was safe and how many days are left to restore it." />
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section id="safety" class="safety wrap" data-reveal>
    <div class="safety-head">
      <h2>It never removes work that exists nowhere else.</h2>
      <p>
        That is the whole job. Every rule below is covered by tests that run against real git repositories, because mocking git
        would hide exactly the cases that lose work.
      </p>
    </div>
    <dl class="rules">
      {safety.map(([what, when]) => (
        <div class="rule">
          <dt>{what}</dt>
          <dd>Only when {when}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section id="install" class="install wrap" data-reveal>
    <div class="install-main">
      <h2>Install</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><a href={links.download}>Download the DMG</a> and open it.</li>
        <li>Drag Lopper onto Applications.</li>
        <li>Open Lopper, pick your project folders, and read the overview.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="muted">
        Needs macOS 14 or later and git (<code>xcode-select --install</code>). The GitHub CLI is optional and adds pull
        request based merge detection.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href={links.download}>Download for macOS</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href={links.install}>Full install guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="install-side">
      <h3>The first launch</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        macOS asks you to confirm apps that are not notarized yet. Right-click Lopper in Applications, choose Open, then Open
        again. Or run this once:
      </p>
      <pre><code>xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Lopper.app</code></pre>
      <h3>Build it yourself</h3>
      <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/Zawalid/Lopper.git
cd Lopper &amp;&amp; scripts/build-app.sh</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq wrap" data-reveal>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      {faq.map(([q, a]) => (
        <details>
          <summary>{q}</summary>
          <p>{a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var video = document.getElementById('hero-video');
      var button = document.getElementById('hero-pause');
      if (!video || !button) return;
      function sync() {
        var paused = video.paused;
        button.textContent = paused ? 'Play animation' : 'Pause animation';
        button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', paused ? 'true' : 'false');
      }
      if (matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) { video.removeAttribute('autoplay'); video.pause(); }
      button.addEventListener('click', function () { if (video.paused) { video.play(); } else { video.pause(); } sync(); });
      video.addEventListener('play', sync);
      video.addEventListener('pause', sync);
      sync();
    })();
  </script>

  <style>
    .hero { padding-block: clamp(40px, 7vw, 96px) clamp(24px, 4vw, 56px); background: radial-gradient(60% 50% at 70% 0%, var(--glow), transparent 70%); }
    .hero-grid { display: grid; gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 64px); align-items: center; }
    @media (min-width: 980px) { .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr); } }
    .lede { margin-top: 22px; font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1.6vw, 1.3rem); color: var(--muted); max-width: 34em; }
    .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 30px; }
    .fineprint { margin-top: 18px; font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--faint); }

    .window { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); overflow: hidden; background: var(--surface); }
    .hero-visual video { width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 16 / 10; object-fit: cover; }
    .pause { margin-top: 10px; background: none; border: 0; padding: 4px 0; color: var(--faint); font: 500 0.9rem var(--font-body); cursor: pointer; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 0.2em; }
    .pause:hover { color: var(--text); }

    .why { display: grid; gap: 28px; padding-block: clamp(56px, 8vw, 112px) 0; }
    .why h2 { max-width: 18em; }
    .why-text { display: grid; gap: 18px; color: var(--muted); max-width: 40em; }
    .why-text code { color: var(--text); }
    @media (min-width: 980px) { .why { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 64px; align-items: start; } }

    .features { display: grid; gap: clamp(64px, 9vw, 120px); padding-block: clamp(64px, 9vw, 120px) 0; }
    .band { display: grid; gap: 28px; align-items: center; }
    .band-copy { display: grid; gap: 14px; }
    .band-copy p { color: var(--muted); max-width: 30em; }
    @media (min-width: 980px) {
      .band { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 4.4fr) minmax(0, 7fr); gap: 64px; }
      .band.reverse { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 4.4fr); }
      .band.reverse .band-copy { order: 2; }
    }

    .safety { display: grid; gap: 36px; padding-block: clamp(72px, 10vw, 136px) 0; }
    .safety-head { display: grid; gap: 14px; max-width: 40em; }
    .safety-head p { color: var(--muted); }
    .rules { margin: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .rule { display: grid; gap: 4px; padding: 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .rule dt { font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.15rem; }
    .rule dd { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); }
    @media (min-width: 820px) { .rule { grid-template-columns: 17em 1fr; gap: 32px; align-items: baseline; } }

    .install { display: grid; gap: 40px; padding-block: clamp(72px, 10vw, 136px) 0; }
    @media (min-width: 980px) { .install { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 72px; } }
    .install-main { display: grid; gap: 22px; align-content: start; }
    .steps { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.3em; display: grid; gap: 8px; }
    .muted { color: var(--muted); }
    .install-side { display: grid; gap: 14px; align-content: start; padding: 28px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--surface); }
    .install-side h3:not(:first-child) { margin-top: 12px; }
    pre { margin: 0; padding: 14px 16px; overflow-x: auto; background: var(--surface-2); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.55; }
    pre code { font-family: var(--font-mono); }

    .faq { display: grid; gap: 28px; padding-block: clamp(72px, 10vw, 136px) 0; }
    .faq-list { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
    details { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    summary { list-style: none; cursor: pointer; padding: 20px 0; font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.15rem; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 24px; }
    summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
    summary::after { content: "+"; font-weight: 500; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.4rem; line-height: 1; }
    details[open] summary::after { content: "\2212"; }
    details p { padding-bottom: 22px; color: var(--muted); max-width: 44em; }
  </style>
</Base>
